unary \code{-}. Calls without column names, such as \code{all_of(vars)} or \code{seq_len(2)},
also act as selections.

Other expressions using columns, such as \code{lexp >= 70} or
\code{gnp_thousands = gnppc / 1000}, are computed with \code{\link[dplyr:mutate]{dplyr::mutate()}} and then
selected. Arithmetic is therefore not interpreted as column positions.
Named constants (\code{one = 1}, \code{label = "x"}, \code{y = c(1, 2)}) create columns;
they do not select or rename existing columns by position.

\strong{Names and fallback evaluation}

Unnamed names, strings and positions must identify existing columns. An
